WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.110 --> 00:00:01.620
- So how have you been keeping up.

00:00:01.620 --> 00:00:03.320
So you have "This Is Us," do you all have,

00:00:03.320 --> 00:00:04.600
I know that you get in these casts,

00:00:04.600 --> 00:00:06.360
especially these really successful,

00:00:06.360 --> 00:00:07.940
and y'all are on there for seasons,

00:00:07.940 --> 00:00:08.773
have you all been able to catch up at all?

00:00:08.773 --> 00:00:10.640
Have you all zoomed at
all or done anything?

00:00:10.640 --> 00:00:13.926
- Yeah, so we have done the
Zoom, we have Zoom zoomed.

00:00:13.926 --> 00:00:18.133
And it was so sweet because
Justin Hartley, who plays Kevin,

00:00:19.050 --> 00:00:22.370
he's the one that's like,
"Hey, guys, do you wanna Zoom?"

00:00:22.370 --> 00:00:24.330
And we're like, "Oh!"
(Kelly laughs)

00:00:24.330 --> 00:00:26.950
And that's just Justin,
he's not just a handsome guy

00:00:26.950 --> 00:00:27.900
who's super talented.

00:00:27.900 --> 00:00:30.330
He has the biggest heart,
and so it was so cute

00:00:30.330 --> 00:00:33.010
that he was the one that
wanted to arrange it.

00:00:33.010 --> 00:00:35.810
And then Chris arranged
the actual appointment time

00:00:35.810 --> 00:00:38.240
and called it the Miguel Rivas Fan Club,

00:00:38.240 --> 00:00:41.240
which Jon Huertas plays Miguel, who,

00:00:41.240 --> 00:00:44.060
and everyone there was
like, "No one likes Miguel."

00:00:44.060 --> 00:00:45.790
Jon is the best sport about it all

00:00:45.790 --> 00:00:47.870
because everybody just
makes a joke about it.

00:00:47.870 --> 00:00:49.320
But yeah, it's a lot of fun.

00:00:49.320 --> 00:00:52.670
We just get to sort of see
each other, which is nice.

00:00:52.670 --> 00:00:54.340
It's like the phone calls
aren't quite enough,

00:00:54.340 --> 00:00:55.760
and the text chats aren't-

00:00:55.760 --> 00:00:57.000
- No, the getting to see each other,

00:00:57.000 --> 00:00:59.560
like any kind of Zoom,
or FaceTime, I agree.

00:00:59.560 --> 00:01:00.940
I mean, god, can you imagine

00:01:00.940 --> 00:01:02.580
what this would be like without it?

00:01:02.580 --> 00:01:05.180
Without seeing people,
like just on a phone,

00:01:05.180 --> 00:01:07.700
like in the kitchen with
the Roseanne phone line

00:01:07.700 --> 00:01:10.050
that's like 10-feet long.

00:01:10.050 --> 00:01:11.530
Yeah, that would kill me.

00:01:11.530 --> 00:01:12.363
Yeah.

00:01:12.363 --> 00:01:14.320
- Yeah, it wouldn't be
good, that's for sure.

00:01:14.320 --> 00:01:16.270
So, grateful for technology.

00:01:16.270 --> 00:01:18.360
- Yeah, no, me too.

00:01:18.360 --> 00:01:20.640
So who of your "This Is Us" cast

00:01:20.640 --> 00:01:22.410
seem to be having the
best time in quarantine,

00:01:22.410 --> 00:01:24.780
like when you all talked,
who's living their best life?

00:01:24.780 --> 00:01:26.205
- I think really me.

00:01:26.205 --> 00:01:27.330
Honestly.
(Kelly laughs)

00:01:27.330 --> 00:01:29.915
I have to be honest, I
really like being at home.

00:01:29.915 --> 00:01:31.800
- Oh, you don't have kids right now,

00:01:31.800 --> 00:01:34.140
so that's, oh, there you go, that's why.

00:01:34.140 --> 00:01:35.410
You know what, I'm telling you

00:01:35.410 --> 00:01:36.920
that you're having the best time.

00:01:36.920 --> 00:01:38.020
(Chrissy laughs)

00:01:38.020 --> 00:01:39.220
I don't know about everybody else,

00:01:39.220 --> 00:01:43.020
but I love actually
getting to have the time,

00:01:43.020 --> 00:01:45.250
especially recently, I've
been waking up every morning,

00:01:45.250 --> 00:01:46.810
coloring with them, it's like a lot of

00:01:46.810 --> 00:01:48.960
kind of me time with
them and I've loved that.

00:01:48.960 --> 00:01:51.160
But at the same time,
it's like, "Oh my gosh,

00:01:51.160 --> 00:01:52.680
I really want to go to
a dinner with adults

00:01:52.680 --> 00:01:54.423
and just talk about adult things."

00:01:54.423 --> 00:01:55.363
- Right.

00:01:55.363 --> 00:01:58.190
I mean, I feel for Sterling
'cause he and Ryan,

00:01:58.190 --> 00:02:01.400
he and his wife are obviously
teaching their two sons,

00:02:01.400 --> 00:02:05.220
and he's like, (sighs)
"Man, I gotta run, guys.

00:02:05.220 --> 00:02:06.340
I gotta start class.

00:02:06.340 --> 00:02:08.063
We gotta do this, we gotta that."

00:02:08.063 --> 00:02:08.930
- Oh my gosh.

00:02:08.930 --> 00:02:10.640
- I know. I don't (sigh).

00:02:10.640 --> 00:02:12.630
Listen, I can barely
keep a succulent alive

00:02:12.630 --> 00:02:14.977
that I started having at
the beginning of quarantine.

00:02:14.977 --> 00:02:15.840
- (laughs) Succulents are like

00:02:15.840 --> 00:02:18.660
the easiest plants to keep alive.

00:02:18.660 --> 00:02:20.310
- They don't need anything.

00:02:20.310 --> 00:02:21.380
- I know, that's amazing.

00:02:21.380 --> 00:02:23.180
That's why you're my favorite human.

